# Keep the Docker build context to source only.
#
# Without this file the context is the whole repository, including the sandbox
# runtime directories (`.run/`, several gigabytes of PostgreSQL data, captured
# screenshots and Playwright browser binaries) and every built artefact. That
# makes the context enormous and, worse, lets a stale host `dist/` or `.next/`
# be copied over a fresh build.

# Runtime and audit state — never part of an image.
.run/
backups/
docs/audit/
logs/

# Dependencies and build output are produced inside the image.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
.next/
**/.next/
out/
**/out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Tests, coverage and tooling caches.
coverage/
**/coverage/
playwright-report/
**/playwright-report/
test-results/
**/test-results/
.agent_tmp/
.turbo/

# Local configuration and secrets. `.env.example` is committed; a real `.env`
# or `.env.production` must never enter an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy/env/*.env
!deploy/env/*.example

# Version control and editor metadata.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
.DS_Store

# Deployment material that is mounted, not baked in.
deploy/nginx/certs/
deploy/nginx/logs/
